From ea7d1b1b3de8513ae6e557fe2be93d380eb04874 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Graber?= <stgraber@stgraber.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:53:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] incusd: Don't let an image plant a liblxc config file
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

liblxc loads <lxcpath>/<name>/config and acts on <name>/partial on its
own, and that directory is the instance volume, so an image carrying a
top-level "config" file had it loaded as the container's LXC config,
running its hooks as host root and bypassing the raw.lxc restriction.

Refuse to instantiate a container whose directory holds those entries,
and strip them when filling a container volume.

This addresses GHSA-mmh3-jfjc-6vc2 (CVE pending)

Signed-off-by: Stéphane Graber <stgraber@stgraber.org>
(cherry picked from commit 035b5cf27be400fbba43ca1903593da2682d9c01)
